REID v9.3 — Dual‑Plane License
Public‑Safe Specification + Proprietary Engine Licensing Framework
Enterprise Licensing Edition

====================================================================
1. Overview
====================================================================
This Dual‑Plane License governs the use, distribution, evaluation, and
integration of the REID v9.3 architecture. It separates REID into two
distinct licensing planes:

Plane A — Public Specification (Open License)
Plane B — Proprietary Engine (Restricted License)

This structure allows enterprises such as Microsoft or Google to adopt
the REID architecture safely while preserving proprietary substrate
physics, execution mechanics, and internal algorithms.

====================================================================
2. Plane A — Public Specification License (Apache 2.0)
====================================================================
The following components are licensed under the Apache License 2.0:

• Full REID v9.3 Specification
• All PACK documents (Kernel → UC → CL → IC → API-MAP → INFRA)
• All schemas (Protobuf + OpenAPI)
• All governance documents (Conformance, Epoch Registry, Safety)
• All deployment templates (AKS, Helm, Azure Policy)
• All diagrams and documentation
• All public‑safe architectural structures

Under Apache 2.0, users may:

• Use the specification
• Copy the specification
• Modify the specification
• Distribute the specification
• Build systems based on the specification

Apache 2.0 applies ONLY to Plane A.

====================================================================
3. Plane B — Proprietary Engine License (SEP/RAND)
====================================================================
The following components are NOT open source and are licensed under a
Restricted Engine Plane (SEP) with Reasonable And Non‑Discriminatory
(RAND) terms:

• Substrate physics
• Drift/coherence internal algorithms
• SIL-v9.3 internal lock mechanics
• AAG-v9.3 internal routing mechanics
• Temporal Ledger internal propagation rules
• Binding Chain internal enforcement logic
• Internal governor heuristics
• Internal fallback heuristics
• Internal corpus synthesis mechanics
• Any unpublished PACK internals
• Any future versions (v9.4, v10, etc.)

These components may NOT be:

• Copied
• Modified
• Reverse engineered
• Redistributed
• Disclosed
• Open‑sourced

Plane B requires a formal licensing agreement.

====================================================================
4. Rights Granted Under Plane A (Apache 2.0)
====================================================================
Users may:

• Evaluate the REID architecture
• Integrate REID PACKs into internal systems
• Build products using the public specification
• Extend PACKs for internal use
• Create tooling based on schemas
• Deploy REID in cloud or edge environments

These rights apply ONLY to Plane A.

====================================================================
5. Rights Granted Under Plane B (SEP/RAND)
====================================================================
Upon execution of a licensing agreement, enterprises may:

• Integrate proprietary engine components
• Access internal substrate physics
• Access internal drift/coherence algorithms
• Access SIL/AAG internal mechanics
• Access proprietary temporal propagation rules
• Access proprietary fallback logic
• Access proprietary synthesis logic
• Access proprietary governor logic

These rights require:

• A signed licensing agreement
• Defined scope of use
• Defined exclusivity tier
• Defined support model

====================================================================
6. Rights Retained by the Creator
====================================================================
The creator retains:

• Full ownership of REID architecture
• Full ownership of all PACKs
• Full ownership of all primitives
• Full ownership of all proprietary engine components
• Full ownership of all future versions
• Full rights to license REID to additional partners unless exclusivity is negotiated

No ownership transfer occurs under this license.

====================================================================
7. Exclusivity Options
====================================================================
Tier 1 — Non‑Exclusive  
Tier 2 — Sector Exclusive  
Tier 3 — Full Exclusive  

Exclusivity applies ONLY to Plane B.

====================================================================
8. Prohibited Actions
====================================================================
Users may NOT:

• Reverse engineer proprietary components
• Attempt to derive substrate physics
• Attempt to derive drift/coherence algorithms
• Attempt to derive SIL/AAG internals
• Attempt to derive temporal propagation rules
• Attempt to derive fallback heuristics
• Attempt to derive synthesis mechanics
• Attempt to derive governor logic
• Claim ownership of REID architecture
• Redistribute proprietary components

Violations terminate the license.

